  "meta": {
    "title": "Why Bolivia Has a Navy but No Sea 🇧🇴🤯 The Lost Coast",
    "description": "Bolivia 🇧🇴 is landlocked, yet it has a navy of about 5,000 personnel ⚓ patrolling Lake Titicaca and rivers. Why? Bolivia used to have a Pacific coast 🌊 In 1879 a tax dispute with a Chilean mining company started the War of the Pacific 🇨🇱 Chile defeated Bolivia and Peru, Bolivia lost its coastal Litoral Department, and Peru lost Tarapacá. Every 23 March Bolivia still marks the Day of the Sea, keeping hope of a coast alive 🤯",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "A navy with no sea 🤯🇧🇴⚓",
      "Should Bolivia get its coast back? 👇",
      "Which lost territory should we explain next? 🗺️"
    ],
